{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Convolutional Weight Sharing.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Convolutional Weight Sharing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"convolutional weight sharing convolutional weight sharing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Convolutional Weight Sharing.md","fileName":"Convolutional Weight Sharing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Convolutional Weight Sharing","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 02:14\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Convolutional Visual Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Convolutional Visual Architecture","CNN Receptive Field","Convolutional Neural Network","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Convolutional Weight Sharing.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Convolutional Weight Sharing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"convolutional weight sharing convolutional weight sharing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Convolutional Weight Sharing.md","fileName":"Convolutional Weight Sharing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Convolutional Weight Sharing","heading":"Convolutional Weight Sharing","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Convolutional weight sharing means that neurons inspecting different image locations use the same learned weights. Because the weights define a detector, those neurons search for the same pattern in different [[CNN Receptive Field|receptive fields]]. A feature can be found wherever a member of the shared group responds, rather than requiring a separately learned detector at each position.\n\nSharing also reduces the number of trainable parameters compared with assigning independent weights to every local neuron. It supplies a useful spatial assumption to a [[Convolutional Neural Network]]: the local pattern worth detecting may recur at multiple locations. Pooling can add tolerance to location, but it can also discard information about the arrangement of parts.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Convolutional Visual Architecture","CNN Receptive Field","Convolutional Neural Network","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Convolutional Weight Sharing.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Convolutional Weight Sharing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"convolutional weight sharing convolutional weight sharing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Convolutional Weight Sharing.md","fileName":"Convolutional Weight Sharing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Convolutional Weight Sharing","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[deeplearning_mit.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Convolutional Visual Architecture","CNN Receptive Field","Convolutional Neural Network","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}